  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: DiscPhys 4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: 'A research team is exploring a new treatment that blocks a protein found
    throughout the body. You point out that blocking this protein could also affect
    healthy functions, raising concerns about possible side effects.


    <b>Why
    is physician input valuable in this situation?</b>'
  explanation: Physicians use their understanding of how the body works to help decide
    which treatment ideas are likely to be safe and helpful. If a treatment blocks
    something the body needs to function normally, it could cause serious side effects
    that outweigh the benefits. By sharing this perspective early, physicians help
    research teams focus on treatment ideas that are not only promising in the lab,
    but also realistic and safe for real people.
  correctAnswer: Helping the research team avoid treatment ideas that could cause
    harmful side effects
  incorrectAnswer1: "Deciding when it\u2019s time to begin safety testing in animals"
  incorrectAnswer2: Changing the structure of the treatment idea itself
  incorrectAnswer3: Choosing which lab tests to use to study the treatment in cells
  questionRole: Physician
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
